 against evil entities in the trans-mundane one. In this sense, Syriac amulets may be interpreted as a ritual/therapeutic tool related to the emotions of people in Late-Antique Mesopotamian multicultural society (4th–7th century AD).</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
